WEBVTT


00:03:56.026 --> 00:04:00.054
Cloud sailers.
New toy cloud sailers.


00:04:37.402 --> 00:04:39.267
Sora. Tumi.


00:04:39.338 --> 00:04:40.566
Welcome.


00:04:40.639 --> 00:04:42.197
Roven, Tumi's still sick.


00:04:42.274 --> 00:04:44.003
Let's have a look.


00:04:58.024 --> 00:05:00.619
- Present.
- Kima?


00:05:00.694 --> 00:05:01.853
Present.


00:05:01.928 --> 00:05:04.295
- Tulo?
- Present.


00:05:04.365 --> 00:05:07.731
- Tumi?
- Present.


00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.063
Senn?


00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.965
Senn?


00:05:13.107 --> 00:05:15.507
Mala?


00:05:15.576 --> 00:05:16.941
Mala?


00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.380
Come on, Senn!


00:05:21.448 --> 00:05:23.382
It's only a race if you keep up.


00:05:29.123 --> 00:05:31.285
Is it my fault you keep cheating?


00:05:31.359 --> 00:05:32.621
I don't cheat.


00:05:36.865 --> 00:05:38.833
Not all the time.


00:05:44.873 --> 00:05:45.932
Classic Mala.


00:05:46.008 --> 00:05:48.067
Great. All right.


00:05:48.144 --> 00:05:49.406
Very funny.
Where are you?


00:05:50.479 --> 00:05:52.106
Bye!


00:05:55.017 --> 00:05:57.679
That was really funny.
You got me... again.


00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.488
Do you hear that?
Is it me?


00:06:05.561 --> 00:06:08.258
I think it's coming
from right below... us!


00:06:15.138 --> 00:06:18.005
See? She doesn't think
much of your flying, either.


00:06:26.451 --> 00:06:27.883
Beautiful.


00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:00.876
Are you thinking what I'm thinking?


00:07:00.954 --> 00:07:02.888
Turn around and go home?


00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:17.870
Hey, Mala? Mala?
Probably not a...


00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:19.404
Wind tunnel!


00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:22.707
Mala, pull up!


00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:25.073
Senn, throw the anchor!


00:07:25.145 --> 00:07:26.703
Mala!


00:07:32.887 --> 00:07:35.617
Come on! Come on!


00:08:00.949 --> 00:08:02.473
Are you thinking what
I'm thinking now?


00:08:02.552 --> 00:08:05.020
'Cause clearly it's time to go back.


00:08:08.724 --> 00:08:10.487
Mala, where are you going?


00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:12.221
Are you crazy?


00:08:12.295 --> 00:08:15.355
Mala, you know this place
is forbidden.


00:08:18.067 --> 00:08:19.534
Wasn't the wind tunnel enough?


00:08:19.602 --> 00:08:22.196
And the huge, crazy sky whale?


00:08:26.876 --> 00:08:28.572
Finally, you've come to your senses.


00:08:28.645 --> 00:08:31.545
Let's go back now, okay?


00:08:31.615 --> 00:08:33.344
Senn?


00:08:33.417 --> 00:08:35.180
What is that?


00:09:10.589 --> 00:09:13.057
Mom, what's that?


00:09:13.125 --> 00:09:14.990
Tumi, come inside.


00:09:38.118 --> 00:09:39.779
A new god!


00:09:40.987 --> 00:09:43.320
A new god in the sky.


00:09:46.559 --> 00:09:50.587
Go home.
The elders will check on you.


00:09:57.805 --> 00:09:59.739
Keep moving.


00:09:59.807 --> 00:10:01.331
Move along.


00:10:02.476 --> 00:10:04.672
All is well.


00:10:04.746 --> 00:10:06.338
It has begun.


00:10:08.449 --> 00:10:10.611
Is everyone safe here?


00:10:10.686 --> 00:10:13.450
Is there anything that you need?


00:11:02.674 --> 00:11:05.438
So, you think it's a god?


00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:07.273
It could be one of those large rocks.


00:11:07.345 --> 00:11:09.210
The kind that fall from the sky
from time to time.


00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:11.713
It will be whatever
the elders tell us it is.


00:11:11.783 --> 00:11:13.648
I bet I could see what it is.


00:11:13.718 --> 00:11:15.948
I bet I could make something
to help me look closer.


00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:18.488
Mala, you know that's forbidden.


00:11:18.556 --> 00:11:20.615
But why?
It wouldn't hurt anybody.


00:11:20.693 --> 00:11:23.218
Inventions that are not approved
by the elders


00:11:23.294 --> 00:11:24.785
are against our teachings.


00:11:24.863 --> 00:11:26.297
Then maybe our teachings are wrong.


00:11:26.365 --> 00:11:29.892
Mala! Go to your room.


00:11:29.969 --> 00:11:31.698
Right now.


00:12:13.213 --> 00:12:15.478
Getting closer.


00:13:19.316 --> 00:13:21.716
What is that?


00:13:31.062 --> 00:13:32.256
No.


00:13:39.338 --> 00:13:40.998
Sound the alarm!


00:13:42.807 --> 00:13:44.776
Everyone, take cover!


00:13:50.016 --> 00:13:51.449
Mala?


00:13:51.517 --> 00:13:54.077
Everyone, get to your homes.


00:13:54.153 --> 00:13:55.415
What is that?


00:13:56.923 --> 00:13:59.392
Mala! Where are you?


00:13:59.458 --> 00:14:00.891
Mala!


00:14:11.872 --> 00:14:14.568
It's a miracle!
They are gods!


00:14:16.043 --> 00:14:19.308
- Yes. Take me.
- No, wait!


00:14:20.847 --> 00:14:22.712
Mala!


00:14:22.783 --> 00:14:24.945
- Over here!
- You see that?


00:14:25.019 --> 00:14:26.280
- Where are you?
- I'm ready!


00:14:26.353 --> 00:14:28.982
Tumi! Tumi, where are you?


00:14:29.057 --> 00:14:31.786
- I am ready!
- I knew this day would come.


00:14:31.858 --> 00:14:33.258
- Take me!
- Over here!


00:14:33.327 --> 00:14:34.761
- Over here!
- Over here!


00:14:34.829 --> 00:14:36.319
Mommy? Mommy?


00:14:36.397 --> 00:14:37.989
Mom, where are you?


00:14:40.635 --> 00:14:42.227
- Oh, no!
- Take me!


00:14:42.304 --> 00:14:45.864
- Everyone please!
- Where's my daughter?


00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.066
Mala?


00:14:47.141 --> 00:14:48.666
Father.


00:14:48.744 --> 00:14:51.542
I'm coming!
Father, look out!


00:14:54.116 --> 00:14:55.879
No! Please!


00:14:55.951 --> 00:14:57.578
Let him go! Take me!


00:14:57.653 --> 00:15:00.623
It's my fault! Please!


00:15:01.891 --> 00:15:04.416
Take me! Over here.


00:15:04.494 --> 00:15:05.482
Please.


00:15:09.065 --> 00:15:10.760
Fine.


00:15:10.834 --> 00:15:12.324
I'll do it my way.


00:15:15.839 --> 00:15:18.364
Come on, take me.
Take me.


00:17:11.961 --> 00:17:13.690
Stay where you are!


00:17:41.625 --> 00:17:43.718
Get away from me...


00:17:43.794 --> 00:17:46.523
you monster.


00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:17.458
Please remain in your homes.


00:18:23.936 --> 00:18:26.667
Remain in your homes
for the time being.


00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:32.141
Stay home!


00:18:35.949 --> 00:18:38.679
Everything is under control.


00:18:57.504 --> 00:18:59.267
Stay home.


00:19:04.144 --> 00:19:06.238
Are you okay? Where's Roven?


00:19:06.313 --> 00:19:08.247
He was taken by the gods.


00:19:08.316 --> 00:19:10.476
Please, Doron, we have to help him.


00:19:10.552 --> 00:19:12.076
They are not gods.


00:19:12.153 --> 00:19:13.780
They are invaders, pretenders.


00:19:13.855 --> 00:19:16.324
Dangerous.


00:19:16.391 --> 00:19:18.188
What about my father?


00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:19.626
How will we get him back?


00:19:19.694 --> 00:19:21.992
We will do the best we can, Mala.


00:19:22.063 --> 00:19:24.657
For now, stay inside.


00:19:36.612 --> 00:19:38.876
Don't touch that!


00:19:38.948 --> 00:19:40.745
Lieutenant Stanton, speak to me.


00:19:40.816 --> 00:19:42.978
Are you still operational?


00:19:44.254 --> 00:19:46.687
Stop it.
Now, now, now.


00:19:46.757 --> 00:19:48.952
There's no need for violence.


00:19:49.026 --> 00:19:50.857
Can't we communicate verbally?


00:19:50.927 --> 00:19:53.794
You speak our language? How?


00:19:53.864 --> 00:19:55.764
I have been programmed
with the basic forms


00:19:55.832 --> 00:19:56.924
of your vernacular, yes.


00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:58.524
Does he speak our language?


00:19:58.603 --> 00:20:00.070
What? No. No, no, no.
Now listen...


00:20:00.137 --> 00:20:02.766
I need to talk to him.
Can you teach me his language?


00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:05.000
Priorities first. He's dying.


00:20:05.075 --> 00:20:07.636
Teach me or I won't help.


00:20:07.712 --> 00:20:09.942
Lieutenant Stanton won't like this.


00:20:11.115 --> 00:20:14.744
Hold still. Now, don't blink.


00:20:24.063 --> 00:20:25.724
My head.


00:20:25.798 --> 00:20:28.357
It's full of words.


00:20:28.433 --> 00:20:31.062
What language is this?
How did you do that?


00:20:31.136 --> 00:20:33.331
A simple organic data download.


00:20:33.405 --> 00:20:36.773
Now, please, you must help,
or he will die.


00:20:36.842 --> 00:20:38.036
Where do I begin?


00:20:38.110 --> 00:20:41.080
Lieutenant Stanton requires oxygen,


00:20:41.146 --> 00:20:42.909
a gaseous chemical element.


00:20:42.981 --> 00:20:44.950
Colorless, odorless, tasteless.


00:20:45.018 --> 00:20:46.508
Vital for respiration.


00:20:46.586 --> 00:20:50.954
We need to seal this room
and construct an air generator.


00:20:51.024 --> 00:20:53.390
We must identify
an oxygen-gathering plant


00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:55.826
and incorporate it into this assembly.


00:20:55.896 --> 00:20:58.921
Please gather all available plant life.


00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:34.433
Hurry. He's beginning to suffocate.


00:21:34.503 --> 00:21:36.767
Please initiate the procedure.


00:21:57.293 --> 00:21:58.760
We did it!


00:22:09.406 --> 00:22:11.134
What the...


00:22:11.207 --> 00:22:12.869
Giddy?


00:22:14.378 --> 00:22:15.970
Where am I?


00:22:16.046 --> 00:22:18.071
In a dwelling used
by the natives of this world.


00:22:18.148 --> 00:22:19.309
I'm a prisoner?


00:22:19.383 --> 00:22:20.816
I would say a guest.


00:22:20.884 --> 00:22:23.979
Then let's not overstay our welcome.
Get me Earth Force.


00:22:24.055 --> 00:22:26.682
Negative.
My transmitter was damaged.


00:22:26.757 --> 00:22:29.852
Great. The ship.
How's my ship?


00:22:29.928 --> 00:22:33.295
Neutronic conductor overloaded,
stabilizing gears fractured.


00:22:33.364 --> 00:22:36.094
Yeah. But can she fly?


00:22:36.167 --> 00:22:37.259
Negative.


00:22:39.505 --> 00:22:42.269
Giddy, it's one of them.


00:22:42.341 --> 00:22:45.401
This female's parental unit
was taken by our scout ships.


00:22:45.478 --> 00:22:48.379
My name is Mala.
Can you help me save my father?


00:22:48.446 --> 00:22:50.881
It... It speaks our language?


00:22:50.950 --> 00:22:52.781
Giddy taught me your language.


00:22:52.851 --> 00:22:54.285
You taught it?


00:22:54.353 --> 00:22:57.049
Hey, Giddy,
I never authorized that.


00:22:57.122 --> 00:23:01.560
My apologies, but it was hard for you
to issue the proper authorization


00:23:01.627 --> 00:23:04.460
due to your asphyxiation.


00:23:04.530 --> 00:23:06.556
Are... Are you being sarcastic?


00:23:06.633 --> 00:23:08.031
Impossible, sir.


00:23:08.101 --> 00:23:09.965
That is not a feature
of my programming.


00:23:15.408 --> 00:23:17.399
A rescue mission.


00:23:22.649 --> 00:23:25.744
Bring my father home, please!


00:23:31.959 --> 00:23:33.358
Lieutenant Stanton!


00:23:34.362 --> 00:23:36.227
Jim, come inside.


00:23:37.231 --> 00:23:38.391
Stop!


00:23:38.466 --> 00:23:40.593
Your lungs can only
withstand this atmosphere


00:23:40.668 --> 00:23:42.431
for approximately 27.6 seconds.


00:23:42.503 --> 00:23:44.335
- Hurry!
- Give or take.


00:23:44.406 --> 00:23:45.771
- I can't breathe.
- Oh, no.


00:23:45.840 --> 00:23:47.034
No!


00:23:50.679 --> 00:23:52.374
Hold on! I'm coming!


00:23:55.450 --> 00:23:57.214
Hold on!


00:23:58.554 --> 00:23:59.578
No!


00:24:02.090 --> 00:24:03.581
Come on.


00:24:07.162 --> 00:24:08.562
Come on.


00:24:11.334 --> 00:24:12.596
Mala, hold on.


00:24:12.669 --> 00:24:14.762
Help is on its way.


00:24:21.144 --> 00:24:23.009
Giddy, pull!


00:25:03.722 --> 00:25:07.181
Please, forgive him.
He is frightened.


00:25:07.259 --> 00:25:08.817
I scare him?


00:25:08.894 --> 00:25:10.657
Everything different scares them.


00:25:10.730 --> 00:25:12.664
They should've never left home.


00:25:12.732 --> 00:25:16.691
I regret to say they have no choice.


00:25:16.769 --> 00:25:20.102
This was their world... Earth,


00:25:20.172 --> 00:25:22.505
a planet of plenty...


00:25:24.144 --> 00:25:26.271
but not without its limits.


00:25:26.346 --> 00:25:28.143
Eventually, humans exhausted


00:25:28.215 --> 00:25:30.683
their world's natural resources.


00:25:30.751 --> 00:25:33.049
Two neighboring planets...
Mars and Venus...


00:25:33.120 --> 00:25:34.747
were terraformed.


00:25:34.821 --> 00:25:36.448
Colonies were established.


00:25:36.523 --> 00:25:40.460
Two centuries later, the colonies
demanded independence.


00:25:40.528 --> 00:25:41.927
It meant war.


00:25:43.130 --> 00:25:45.360
War.


00:25:45.432 --> 00:25:48.026
All three planets were destroyed.


00:25:48.101 --> 00:25:50.969
Everything was destroyed.


00:25:51.038 --> 00:25:53.132
The survivors had only one choice:


00:25:53.207 --> 00:25:55.038
To travel beyond their solar system


00:25:55.109 --> 00:25:58.374
to the nearest life-supporting planet
they could find.


00:25:58.446 --> 00:26:02.177
The journey lasted several generations
and led them here.


00:26:02.251 --> 00:26:04.845
They named this planet Terra.


00:26:33.283 --> 00:26:34.409
Your home?


00:26:38.823 --> 00:26:42.280
You made this? For me?


00:26:45.996 --> 00:26:49.796
Synchronous rotations,
balance in the focal points.


00:26:49.867 --> 00:26:52.597
This is really good.
Where did you learn to do this?


00:26:52.670 --> 00:26:56.470
All I did was put the pieces together.
They felt right.


00:26:56.540 --> 00:26:59.737
You're a natural.


00:26:59.810 --> 00:27:01.607
Synchronous rotations.


00:27:01.679 --> 00:27:05.740
Stabilizing gears fractured!


00:27:05.816 --> 00:27:06.977
You can...


00:27:07.052 --> 00:27:08.746
Help me repair the ship,


00:27:08.819 --> 00:27:11.789
and I'll take you to your father.


00:27:13.258 --> 00:27:14.748
Deal?


00:27:55.669 --> 00:28:00.003
According to my holographic blueprint,
this device meets all required specifications


00:28:00.073 --> 00:28:03.168
for space travel, approximately.


00:28:06.213 --> 00:28:09.240
Well, it's not exactly titanium,


00:28:09.316 --> 00:28:12.377
but if this thing holds,


00:28:12.453 --> 00:28:13.681
I can go home.


00:28:13.755 --> 00:28:15.689
Remember, we have a deal.


00:28:22.064 --> 00:28:24.623
What is this?


00:28:24.699 --> 00:28:27.669
The Ceremony of Life.


00:28:27.736 --> 00:28:30.899
We thank life for what it brings.


00:28:30.973 --> 00:28:32.941
Even if it brings you war?


00:28:36.512 --> 00:28:39.504
Earth Force recruited me
when I was eight.


00:28:39.582 --> 00:28:41.676
<i>They recruit every kid
on the Ark.</i>


00:28:41.751 --> 00:28:44.879
Intensive training,
hand-to-hand combat,


00:28:44.955 --> 00:28:47.218
flight simulation.


00:28:47.290 --> 00:28:50.418
Be prepared, always on the ready.


00:28:50.493 --> 00:28:54.020
The best, the finest,
the last line of defense.


00:28:55.298 --> 00:28:59.098
You wouldn't understand.


00:28:59.169 --> 00:29:01.195
You only know peace.


00:29:07.111 --> 00:29:08.100
Senn.


00:29:08.178 --> 00:29:09.806
- What are you...
- I had to see you.


00:29:09.881 --> 00:29:12.247
You've locked yourself up for a week.
What's going on?


00:29:12.316 --> 00:29:14.876
- Huh?
- Look, I know how you must feel.


00:29:14.952 --> 00:29:17.477
- But I miss you.
- I miss you, too.


00:29:17.555 --> 00:29:20.116
I just... I need a little time.
Please go.


00:29:20.192 --> 00:29:22.455
Mala, the Ceremony of Life started.
Are we still going together?


00:29:23.695 --> 00:29:25.287
What's that noise?


00:29:25.363 --> 00:29:27.355
- Did you make a new toy for Tuki?
- Senn, wait.


00:29:27.432 --> 00:29:29.332
I knew you were working on something.


00:29:35.474 --> 00:29:37.806
- Mala, run!
- Stop! Stop! You're killing him!


00:29:39.077 --> 00:29:41.011
- I'll take him...
- No!


00:29:45.150 --> 00:29:46.174
I'm okay now.


00:29:46.251 --> 00:29:48.311
- Please, listen.
- It's one of them!


00:29:48.388 --> 00:29:51.789
- I know.
- What? You know?


00:29:51.858 --> 00:29:54.156
- We can't let him go.
- He's my friend!


00:29:54.227 --> 00:29:56.195
- He'll betray us.
- That's enough!


00:29:56.262 --> 00:29:57.992
Mala, what... what have you done?


00:29:58.065 --> 00:30:00.761
He said he would save my father.


00:30:00.834 --> 00:30:01.993
Senn.


00:30:02.068 --> 00:30:03.798
Senn!


00:30:06.272 --> 00:30:07.706
She protected us, Giddy.


00:30:07.775 --> 00:30:10.642
She defended us against her own kind.


00:30:10.711 --> 00:30:12.702
"She"?


00:30:12.780 --> 00:30:15.181
You said "she," not "it."


00:30:15.249 --> 00:30:18.844
We have to go.
He'll be back... with company.


00:30:28.896 --> 00:30:31.195
- What's wrong, Senn?
- It's Mala.


00:30:31.266 --> 00:30:33.427
It's Mala.
She's protecting one of them.


00:30:33.501 --> 00:30:36.402
There's one of those invaders
in her house.


00:30:53.422 --> 00:30:54.411
They were just here.


00:30:55.558 --> 00:30:57.958
Did she build that?


00:30:59.628 --> 00:31:02.826
I believe she did.
Search the home.


00:31:03.967 --> 00:31:05.593
Find them.


00:31:22.086 --> 00:31:24.349
Hey, all clear.


00:31:40.638 --> 00:31:43.506
The elders say a long time ago,


00:31:43.574 --> 00:31:45.872
we were apart from nature.


00:31:45.943 --> 00:31:47.377
We almost died.


00:31:49.247 --> 00:31:51.216
But now we're together,


00:31:51.283 --> 00:31:54.377
forever, in life.


00:31:54.453 --> 00:31:56.478
Fascinating.


00:32:10.837 --> 00:32:13.169
What are those big things
up in the sky, Mom?


00:32:16.242 --> 00:32:17.800
Look!


00:32:17.877 --> 00:32:19.344
Mala!


00:32:28.656 --> 00:32:31.250
Stop it! I'm over here!


00:32:31.325 --> 00:32:32.383
Cease fire!


00:32:34.663 --> 00:32:35.754
Damn it! Stop!


00:32:40.068 --> 00:32:43.469
Hold your fire! I'm over here!


00:32:52.414 --> 00:32:54.974
Why? Why are they doing this?


00:32:55.050 --> 00:32:59.488
I don't know.
It wasn't supposed to be this way.


00:33:35.125 --> 00:33:38.060
Are you sure this is the place?


00:33:38.128 --> 00:33:39.652
It was right here.


00:33:41.766 --> 00:33:44.132
Traces under the recent snow layer
suggest our craft


00:33:44.201 --> 00:33:46.965
has been relocated from its position.


00:33:47.037 --> 00:33:49.598
Someone took it.


00:34:08.294 --> 00:34:10.228
Mala, come on! Keep up!


00:34:18.070 --> 00:34:19.867
Strange.


00:34:19.939 --> 00:34:22.100
This whole place kind
of gives me the creeps.


00:34:22.174 --> 00:34:25.473
The strangeness is increasing.


00:34:39.126 --> 00:34:41.458
What is all this?


00:34:47.134 --> 00:34:50.933
Lieutenant Stanton, all signs indicate
the trail leads through there.


00:35:11.326 --> 00:35:14.261
Those cloud sailers...
what are they doing?


00:35:14.329 --> 00:35:17.493
Not celebrating life,
that's for sure.


00:35:46.597 --> 00:35:48.394
War.


00:35:48.465 --> 00:35:51.263
I guess our species have
more in common than we thought.


00:36:13.792 --> 00:36:15.817
Hey, come on.


00:36:15.894 --> 00:36:19.023
- Where are we going?
- Hitching a ride.


00:36:36.917 --> 00:36:40.079
All right! There's my baby.


00:36:40.152 --> 00:36:43.520
Looks like they're trying
to figure out how it works.


00:36:43.589 --> 00:36:45.716
Cockpit's still locked, though,
so we got a chance to...


00:36:45.792 --> 00:36:47.123
Jim...


00:36:47.194 --> 00:36:49.992
Put down your weapon.
You're surrounded.


00:36:50.063 --> 00:36:52.031
Oh, no.


00:36:54.167 --> 00:36:56.567
- Stop! Back off, or I'll kill her!
- Jim!


00:36:56.636 --> 00:36:58.126
- Jim!
- Play along.


00:36:58.205 --> 00:36:59.695
No! What are you doing?


00:36:59.773 --> 00:37:01.867
- Jim!
- Giddy, now!


00:37:01.942 --> 00:37:03.774
- On my way.
- No! Let me go!


00:37:06.981 --> 00:37:09.449
I said get back!


00:37:18.827 --> 00:37:20.988
Come on, Mala.
They can't see you.


00:37:21.063 --> 00:37:23.496
- You can stop fighting now.
- You said you'd kill me.


00:37:23.564 --> 00:37:25.156
It was just an act, Mala.


00:37:25.234 --> 00:37:27.168
I was just pretending.
I wouldn't hurt you.


00:37:27.235 --> 00:37:28.601
Honestly.


00:37:28.670 --> 00:37:29.967
Stop him!


00:37:30.038 --> 00:37:32.836
- Hurry, Giddy! Hurry!
- Coming.


00:37:35.844 --> 00:37:37.402
Open the hatch.


00:37:40.450 --> 00:37:41.677
Thank you.


00:37:44.554 --> 00:37:46.647
You can do it.
Come on. Hold it together.


00:37:48.024 --> 00:37:50.150
Come on, baby. Come on.


00:37:51.995 --> 00:37:55.624
- Not good?
- No. Very not good.


00:37:57.500 --> 00:38:00.196
- What the...
- Uh-oh.


00:38:08.279 --> 00:38:11.680
- Time to go?
- Come on. Just one spark.


00:38:19.724 --> 00:38:22.692
All right! There we go!


00:38:22.760 --> 00:38:24.558
Come on, Giddy.
We're going home.


00:38:27.532 --> 00:38:30.227
Hold tight, okay?
This could be a bumpy ride.


00:39:12.212 --> 00:39:15.147
Your people... they made this?


00:39:15.215 --> 00:39:18.616
Yeah. Don't let her looks fool you.


00:39:18.685 --> 00:39:21.381
She hasn't aged too well.


00:39:21.455 --> 00:39:25.118
Central Control,
this is Lieutenant James Stanton.


00:39:25.192 --> 00:39:27.354
Requesting permission to land.


00:39:27.428 --> 00:39:28.452
Lieutenant Stanton.


00:39:28.530 --> 00:39:30.794
Nice of you to finally find
your way back to us.


00:39:30.865 --> 00:39:33.800
Just had myself
some shore leave, that's all.


00:39:33.868 --> 00:39:36.666
You're cleared for landing in Deck A.


00:39:36.738 --> 00:39:38.069
Alert! Alert!


00:39:38.140 --> 00:39:40.370
We have depressurization on Deck C!


00:39:40.442 --> 00:39:42.409
Seal the hatches!
Hull breach!


00:39:42.477 --> 00:39:45.140
No. Not again.


00:39:46.482 --> 00:39:48.574
Welcome to my world.


00:40:02.831 --> 00:40:05.630
Activate cockpit shield.


00:40:10.640 --> 00:40:11.629
Hold on, Mala.


00:40:11.709 --> 00:40:14.142
You have to stay here, okay?
It's not safe.


00:40:14.210 --> 00:40:17.270
Jim, I didn't come all this way to hide.
I have to find my father.


00:40:17.347 --> 00:40:19.679
I understand.
I'll take you to him, I promise.


00:40:19.749 --> 00:40:23.846
But you have to trust me.
I'll be right back.


00:40:23.921 --> 00:40:26.754
Please try not to touch anything, Mala.


00:40:37.735 --> 00:40:40.762
How did you survive your crash?


00:40:40.839 --> 00:40:45.207
After my ship went down,
I woke up to find I'd been rescued and...


00:40:45.276 --> 00:40:46.904
By whom?


00:40:46.979 --> 00:40:48.411
A native.


00:40:48.480 --> 00:40:50.675
Are the natives hostile?


00:40:50.749 --> 00:40:52.081
No.


00:40:52.150 --> 00:40:54.141
Do they have weapons?


00:40:54.219 --> 00:40:56.016
Yes.


00:40:56.088 --> 00:40:59.387
Advanced weapons?


00:41:08.266 --> 00:41:11.794
"I'll be right back," he says.


00:41:57.318 --> 00:41:59.378
Oh, no! Mala!


00:42:04.159 --> 00:42:07.129
Hey, Jim. I missed you, bro.


00:42:07.195 --> 00:42:09.027
Stewart.


00:42:09.098 --> 00:42:10.861
I thought you were a goner.


00:42:10.933 --> 00:42:14.630
Come on. It takes more than
one rough landing to kill me.


00:42:14.704 --> 00:42:18.003
Mom and Dad would be really proud of you.


00:42:18.074 --> 00:42:20.635
You're the man of the hour, Jim.


00:42:20.710 --> 00:42:23.077
I mean, even General Hemmer
wants to meet you.


00:42:23.146 --> 00:42:24.773
Hemmer?


00:42:24.847 --> 00:42:26.577
12 dead.


00:42:26.650 --> 00:42:28.777
A dozen human beings.


00:42:28.852 --> 00:42:31.878
One tarnished, worn-out security seal


00:42:31.955 --> 00:42:35.914
way past its recall date, and gone...


00:42:35.992 --> 00:42:39.019
12 valuable, productive lives.


00:42:39.096 --> 00:42:41.621
How much longer do we have to wait


00:42:41.698 --> 00:42:45.157
while this tomb crumbles around us?


00:42:45.236 --> 00:42:48.227
When will this council
give me the authority


00:42:48.306 --> 00:42:50.103
to do what must be done?


00:42:50.174 --> 00:42:53.940
Your plan calls for nothing less
than the conquest of Terra...


00:42:54.011 --> 00:42:57.846
an alien world, an occupied world.


00:42:57.916 --> 00:42:59.883
My plan, Mr. President,


00:42:59.952 --> 00:43:02.749
is the only way to salvage our species.


00:43:02.820 --> 00:43:05.619
We are dying.


00:43:05.691 --> 00:43:08.626
We are the last relics of humanity.


00:43:08.694 --> 00:43:11.254
The future depends on us.


00:43:15.134 --> 00:43:18.969
We will have no future
if we repeat the mistakes of the past.


00:43:19.037 --> 00:43:21.631
We have superior technology and firepower,


00:43:21.708 --> 00:43:24.040
impenetrable defenses.


00:43:24.110 --> 00:43:27.102
The mistake would be not to act.


00:43:27.179 --> 00:43:30.172
Your plan's under consideration, General.


00:43:30.250 --> 00:43:32.480
We will vote on it.


00:43:32.552 --> 00:43:36.284
Vote! I ask for action, they vote.


00:43:36.357 --> 00:43:38.722
What can we expect from civilians, sir?


00:43:38.792 --> 00:43:40.784
You're a good soldier, Stewart,


00:43:40.861 --> 00:43:43.921
and, I understand,
a brother of a war hero.


00:43:43.998 --> 00:43:46.899
Thank you, sir, but I'm no hero.


00:43:46.966 --> 00:43:48.867
At ease, Lieutenant.


00:43:48.936 --> 00:43:52.201
You're the first man
to distinguish himself in this conflict.


00:43:52.274 --> 00:43:54.503
Congratulations.


00:43:54.576 --> 00:43:57.067
I've had my eye on you for a while.


00:43:57.145 --> 00:44:00.170
James Stanton, 32nd Airborne.


00:44:00.248 --> 00:44:01.976
How many left in the 32nd?


00:44:02.049 --> 00:44:03.381
Eight, sir.


00:44:03.451 --> 00:44:06.249
One short of a baseball team.


00:44:06.321 --> 00:44:07.982
Let me guess.


00:44:08.056 --> 00:44:11.082
Oxygen leaks, faulty fuel lines.


00:44:11.159 --> 00:44:13.218
Engine failure?


00:44:13.295 --> 00:44:17.096
Tired of watching comrades die for nothing?


00:44:17.165 --> 00:44:21.330
We've come a long way.
Terra is our prize.


00:44:21.404 --> 00:44:23.496
A jewel hanging in space.


00:44:23.572 --> 00:44:27.100
It has real water,
not that chemical junk, and ground.


00:44:27.176 --> 00:44:31.078
God, I'd like to feel steady ground
under my feet one day.


00:44:31.147 --> 00:44:34.514
<i>Kids born on the Ark
have never seen a blade of grass</i>


00:44:34.584 --> 00:44:37.109
or heard a bird sing.


00:44:37.186 --> 00:44:38.949
Have you met the enemy?


00:44:39.021 --> 00:44:41.785
I have encountered
the native Terrians, yes, sir.


00:44:43.059 --> 00:44:44.083
What are they like?


00:44:44.160 --> 00:44:46.185
They're an interesting species, sir.


00:44:46.262 --> 00:44:48.697
They're peaceful and they're intelligent.


00:44:48.765 --> 00:44:51.165
Their lives are filled with art and music.


00:44:51.235 --> 00:44:53.294
I meant, can they fight?


00:44:53.370 --> 00:44:56.066
They're not going to hit us
with paintings, are they?


00:44:57.341 --> 00:44:59.901
- I believe they can fight, sir.
- Good.


00:44:59.977 --> 00:45:02.002
Then they'll die with honor.


00:45:10.121 --> 00:45:11.611
Giddy.


00:45:41.922 --> 00:45:45.288
Don't be afraid.
I'll get you out of here.


00:46:11.619 --> 00:46:13.985
Mala.


00:46:14.055 --> 00:46:15.147
Father!


00:46:15.222 --> 00:46:17.782
Father, I'm so sorry.


00:46:17.858 --> 00:46:20.224
I'm gonna get you out of here.


00:46:22.397 --> 00:46:23.955
Hey! A floater!


00:46:27.034 --> 00:46:29.003
This is General Hemmer. Report.


00:46:29.071 --> 00:46:31.198
We have a Terrian floater in Section D, sir.


00:46:31.273 --> 00:46:32.331
Mala.


00:46:34.743 --> 00:46:36.211
Get her!


00:46:38.647 --> 00:46:40.205
I love you.


00:46:49.058 --> 00:46:50.685
Father! Father!


00:46:54.764 --> 00:46:56.664
Father, no!


00:47:12.984 --> 00:47:14.918
Here is your proof that Terrians


00:47:14.985 --> 00:47:17.318
are a hostile, murderous species.


00:47:17.389 --> 00:47:20.186
Two more human lives lost.


00:47:20.257 --> 00:47:22.191
According to Lieutenant Stanton's report,


00:47:22.260 --> 00:47:24.352
the Terrian was seeking its parent,


00:47:24.429 --> 00:47:26.226
one of the abductees.


00:47:26.297 --> 00:47:28.287
The lines have been drawn.


00:47:28.366 --> 00:47:31.529
We are human, they are alien.


00:47:31.603 --> 00:47:34.197
Do not take sides against your own species.


00:47:34.272 --> 00:47:36.866
General, our species has other options.


00:47:36.941 --> 00:47:39.501
We need time to explore, to think,


00:47:39.577 --> 00:47:41.546
before we rush headlong into...


00:47:41.613 --> 00:47:44.640
We have no more time.


00:47:44.716 --> 00:47:47.914
I have waited patiently
for this council to act,


00:47:47.987 --> 00:47:51.923
but our people are tired of dying
in the rotting hull of this ark!


00:47:51.991 --> 00:47:56.292
Therefore, I am assuming command.


00:47:56.363 --> 00:47:58.422
The council is hereby dissolved.


00:47:58.498 --> 00:48:01.022
You do not have the authority, General!


00:48:01.100 --> 00:48:05.435
If I sin, let future generations judge me.


00:48:05.504 --> 00:48:08.065
But mark this: Only thanks to me


00:48:08.141 --> 00:48:10.575
will there be any future generations.


00:48:14.381 --> 00:48:17.214
Hey, Jim, where you going, man?


00:48:17.284 --> 00:48:19.276
- This is wrong.
- Wrong?


00:48:19.353 --> 00:48:21.480
- General Hemmer says...
- How can you follow him?


00:48:21.556 --> 00:48:23.922
- We're soldiers.
- I obey my commanding officer.


00:48:23.990 --> 00:48:26.357
Hey, we obey the council.


00:48:26.427 --> 00:48:29.760
Lieutenant Stanton, I would like you
to join the attack force.


00:48:29.831 --> 00:48:33.028
Respectfully, sir, I refuse.


00:48:33.101 --> 00:48:35.092
You're our only war hero.


00:48:35.170 --> 00:48:36.966
It's your duty to lead the way.


00:48:37.038 --> 00:48:39.029
I lived with the Terrians, sir.


00:48:39.108 --> 00:48:40.904
They're more like us than you can imagine.


00:48:40.976 --> 00:48:42.739
Would it change your decision if I told you


00:48:42.811 --> 00:48:47.510
<i>we only have air on the Ark
for another two months?</i>


00:48:47.583 --> 00:48:52.145
This is mankind's last hope...
the terraformer.


00:48:52.221 --> 00:48:55.123
<i>Currently, it provides
sufficient oxygen for the Ark.</i>


00:48:55.190 --> 00:48:56.953
Once rooted in Terra's surface,


00:48:57.025 --> 00:49:00.553
it will convert the planet
to breathable air within seven days.


00:49:00.630 --> 00:49:02.860
Seven days, Jim.


00:49:02.932 --> 00:49:05.729
Very Biblical, don't you think?


00:49:05.802 --> 00:49:08.828
<i>The Ark will have residual air left
for several more weeks,</i>


00:49:08.905 --> 00:49:10.998
but within that timeframe,


00:49:11.074 --> 00:49:13.008
we will have won ourselves a planet.


00:49:13.076 --> 00:49:14.873
What about the Terrians?


00:49:15.913 --> 00:49:17.311
End hologram.


00:49:19.082 --> 00:49:20.072
What?


00:49:20.150 --> 00:49:21.345
Hello?


00:49:21.418 --> 00:49:22.715
Mala!


00:49:22.786 --> 00:49:24.720
Hello?


00:49:24.788 --> 00:49:27.689
The alien cannot see or hear us.
Don't worry.


00:49:27.758 --> 00:49:30.386
The air is pressurized
for Terrian atmosphere.


00:49:30.461 --> 00:49:32.190
It can breathe.


00:49:32.263 --> 00:49:35.027
A human, however, cannot.


00:49:35.099 --> 00:49:37.091
Anybody there?


00:49:37.168 --> 00:49:39.603
Hello?


00:49:39.670 --> 00:49:40.660
Stewart?


00:49:42.706 --> 00:49:46.507
Where's Jim?
Do you know who Jim is?


00:49:46.578 --> 00:49:49.342
- Where are we?
- Stewart!


00:49:49.414 --> 00:49:52.281
- I can't breathe.
- Somebody help me!


00:49:52.350 --> 00:49:55.081
- Why?
- A test, son.


00:49:55.153 --> 00:49:57.587
The ultimate test.
Whose side are you on?


00:49:57.657 --> 00:49:58.783
Please, say something!


00:50:00.458 --> 00:50:02.016
Stop! You're killing him!


00:50:02.093 --> 00:50:04.391
No. You are.


00:50:04.463 --> 00:50:06.727
Press that red button,
and you can save him.


00:50:06.799 --> 00:50:09.427
A demonstration of the terraforming
technique will commence.


00:50:09.502 --> 00:50:12.370
Your brother will breathe.


00:50:12.438 --> 00:50:14.406
The Terrian will not.


00:50:14.474 --> 00:50:16.135
Hello! Somebody, please help!


00:50:16.210 --> 00:50:17.733
There's gotta be another way.


00:50:17.810 --> 00:50:21.645
There isn't. Us or them.


00:50:21.715 --> 00:50:24.240
- Somebody, he's suffocating!
- Decide.


00:50:24.318 --> 00:50:26.252
I can't breathe.


00:50:29.323 --> 00:50:30.722
Somebody, please help!


00:50:45.406 --> 00:50:47.306
Get away from me!


00:50:47.375 --> 00:50:49.400
What's happening?


00:50:56.517 --> 00:50:59.078
Help! I can't breathe!


00:51:01.656 --> 00:51:03.419
Help!


00:51:03.491 --> 00:51:05.323
I can't breathe!


00:51:05.394 --> 00:51:07.555
I c...


00:51:07.629 --> 00:51:10.394
Giddy, save Mala.


00:51:10.466 --> 00:51:11.899
Confirm order.


00:51:11.967 --> 00:51:14.630
Save Mala.


00:51:16.972 --> 00:51:18.270
What's that robot doing?


00:51:18.340 --> 00:51:20.706
- Otham. Cotters.
- Get down!


00:51:25.949 --> 00:51:28.179
Mala, your respirator.


00:51:29.386 --> 00:51:30.512
Giddy.


00:51:30.587 --> 00:51:32.521
This way.


00:51:34.624 --> 00:51:38.560
- Mala.
- You?


00:51:38.628 --> 00:51:41.530
I'm sorry.


00:51:42.966 --> 00:51:44.935
Mala, hurry.


00:51:49.307 --> 00:51:51.298
- Giddy...
- Follow me.


00:51:51.375 --> 00:51:54.139
- Over there!
- This way has a far lower mortality rate.


00:51:54.211 --> 00:51:55.872
Stop 'em!


00:52:11.763 --> 00:52:15.722
Mala, use the control stick.
Fire missiles... now!


00:52:26.512 --> 00:52:27.570
Incoming missiles!


00:52:40.627 --> 00:52:42.753
Mala, stay calm.


00:52:44.464 --> 00:52:47.434
We're falling too fast!


00:52:49.135 --> 00:52:50.728
Prepare to eject.


00:52:53.808 --> 00:52:55.935
Mala, grab onto my tail.


00:53:01.215 --> 00:53:02.205
Oh, no!


00:53:48.298 --> 00:53:51.062
Hey. About time you joined us.


00:53:53.036 --> 00:53:56.028
Although, now that you're awake, um,
I don't really know what to say.


00:53:56.106 --> 00:53:59.803
I never should've told Doron
about the invader.


00:53:59.876 --> 00:54:03.404
Mala, you're my best friend,
and I should've trusted you.


00:54:03.481 --> 00:54:04.709
I'm sorry.


00:54:04.782 --> 00:54:06.716
I'm sorry, too.


00:54:11.189 --> 00:54:13.919
- Where's Giddy?
- The creature you were with?


00:54:13.992 --> 00:54:15.653
It's being held captive by the elders.


00:54:15.727 --> 00:54:17.388
I have to save him.


00:54:17.463 --> 00:54:20.192
I'm afraid I can't allow that.


00:54:20.264 --> 00:54:21.425
He's a tool of the enemy.


00:54:21.500 --> 00:54:24.435
I can't release him,
but I can take you to him.


00:54:27.673 --> 00:54:29.641
What is this place?


00:54:29.708 --> 00:54:33.610
Our past and possibly our future.


00:54:33.679 --> 00:54:34.976
Warships?


00:54:36.849 --> 00:54:41.218
We came close to destroying ourselves.


00:54:41.287 --> 00:54:46.019
A small group of survivors
formed the eldership.


00:54:46.091 --> 00:54:49.391
They vowed to keep the past a secret


00:54:49.462 --> 00:54:52.898
and build a peaceful future.


00:54:52.967 --> 00:54:56.163
But even gentle beings
must defend themselves when attacked.


00:55:01.242 --> 00:55:04.177
We've been watching the newcomers,


00:55:04.245 --> 00:55:08.079
but we know nothing of their plans
or intentions.


00:55:12.786 --> 00:55:16.985
You're the only one who has
been inside and returned.


00:55:17.058 --> 00:55:20.254
No, I'm not the only one.


00:55:20.327 --> 00:55:22.421
Please, help.


00:55:22.496 --> 00:55:24.397
- Giddy!
- Honestly!


00:55:24.466 --> 00:55:27.299
- What are you doing to him?
- We must dissect it to see how it works.


00:55:27.368 --> 00:55:31.032
- Oh, dear.
- He is my friend. He saved my life.


00:55:31.106 --> 00:55:33.939
Actually, Lieutenant Stanton saved your life.


00:55:34.009 --> 00:55:37.104
- He ordered me to protect you.
- Jim?


00:55:38.581 --> 00:55:41.482
- I must say, this is not very pleasant.
- Leave him alone!


00:55:41.550 --> 00:55:44.018
We need information on the enemy's
strength and numbers.


00:55:44.086 --> 00:55:47.920
- This machine might hold the answer.
- So ask him, don't torture him.


00:55:47.990 --> 00:55:50.550
Will you help us?


00:55:50.627 --> 00:55:52.184
I cannot.


00:55:52.261 --> 00:55:53.785
Earth Force created me.


00:55:53.863 --> 00:55:56.024
Jim commanded you to protect me.


00:55:56.098 --> 00:55:58.931
- Will you disobey his orders?
- Negative.


00:55:59.001 --> 00:56:02.402
But if Earth Force invades,
they'll destroy all life on this world,


00:56:02.472 --> 00:56:04.599
including me.


00:56:04.675 --> 00:56:07.075
Affirmative.


00:56:07.144 --> 00:56:11.478
So the only way to protect me
is to help us defeat Earth Force.


00:56:12.649 --> 00:56:15.948
Well, if... Mala, l...


00:56:16.019 --> 00:56:19.011
Lieutenant Stanton...


00:56:19.090 --> 00:56:22.321
Your logic is tricky, difficult to compute.


00:56:25.630 --> 00:56:27.120
I will protect you.


00:56:35.873 --> 00:56:38.671
Hey, Jim, look, I'm sorry
about what happened


00:56:38.743 --> 00:56:40.335
in the enviro-chamber,
but Hemmer said...


00:56:40.412 --> 00:56:42.676
How can you defend him, even now?


00:56:42.748 --> 00:56:44.773
He said it was the only way


00:56:44.850 --> 00:56:49.719
that we could be sure of your loyalties.


00:56:50.923 --> 00:56:52.323
Sir!


00:56:54.527 --> 00:56:55.892
My apologies, sir.


00:56:55.961 --> 00:56:59.453
I believe the Terrian must have
reprogrammed my robot


00:56:59.531 --> 00:57:01.159
during our captivity.


00:57:01.234 --> 00:57:05.534
Like you said, interesting species.


00:57:05.605 --> 00:57:08.836
Full of surprises.


00:57:08.908 --> 00:57:12.139
We've got a few surprises
up our sleeve, too.


00:57:12.212 --> 00:57:15.010
You're on the terraforming campaign,
Lieutenant.


00:57:15.081 --> 00:57:18.051
- That's an order.
- Sir!


00:57:22.890 --> 00:57:24.949
I don't know what happened
to you on Terra,


00:57:25.026 --> 00:57:27.051
but this is war,


00:57:27.128 --> 00:57:29.858
and I'd feel a lot better
knowing you had my back.


00:57:29.930 --> 00:57:32.194
I've always looked out for you, kid.


00:57:32.266 --> 00:57:34.131
I always will.


00:57:34.201 --> 00:57:37.693
Question is, will Hemmer?


00:58:34.733 --> 00:58:37.701
The aliens breathe something called oxygen,


00:58:37.769 --> 00:58:39.759
so our atmosphere is poisonous to them.


00:58:39.837 --> 00:58:41.362
We must strike early while we...


00:58:41.439 --> 00:58:43.498
And that's where the terraformer should land.


00:58:43.574 --> 00:58:46.135
The formations of oxygen
can spread more rapidly


00:58:46.211 --> 00:58:49.112
to the native population centers,
neutralizing them.


00:58:49.179 --> 00:58:52.149
Air filters here and here


00:58:52.217 --> 00:58:54.208
can alter your atmosphere into oxygen...


00:58:54.285 --> 00:58:56.083
Before the enemy can strike the terraformer,


00:58:56.155 --> 00:59:00.751
we must engage and destroy
their primitive aerial attack force.


00:59:04.163 --> 00:59:06.631
Men and women of Earth Force,


00:59:06.699 --> 00:59:11.033
you hold the entire future of our species
in your hands.


00:59:11.103 --> 00:59:13.094
Brothers and sisters,


00:59:13.173 --> 00:59:15.367
we are engaged in a struggle for survival.


00:59:15.441 --> 00:59:18.808
Not only our own, but for our world.


00:59:18.878 --> 00:59:23.646
Every living being on our planet
depends on us.


00:59:23.717 --> 00:59:27.380
If we fail, we fail them, too.


00:59:28.755 --> 00:59:31.451
Your actions over the next few hours


00:59:31.525 --> 00:59:34.324
will either win ourselves a new home


00:59:34.395 --> 00:59:36.828
or doom us to extinction.


00:59:36.897 --> 00:59:39.389
I believe... I must believe


00:59:39.467 --> 00:59:41.331
that in our darkest hour,


00:59:41.402 --> 00:59:44.928
the very qualities which made us great
will make us strong...


00:59:45.005 --> 00:59:50.137
that love and mercy can triumph
over hate and violence once more.


00:59:50.211 --> 00:59:53.203
Be loyal, be brave.


00:59:53.281 --> 00:59:58.413
Remember who you are
and what you fight for...


00:59:58.487 --> 01:00:00.318
Terra!


01:00:02.791 --> 01:00:06.521
- Hey, take care of yourself up there.
- You, too, Jim.


01:00:43.701 --> 01:00:47.228
- Are you ready?
- No, not really.


01:01:10.028 --> 01:01:11.155
Return fire!


01:01:19.070 --> 01:01:20.060
Down!


01:01:20.139 --> 01:01:23.107
The Terrians are flying new ships
with more powerful weapons.


01:01:23.175 --> 01:01:26.303
No one said we wouldn't
suffer casualties, Lieutenant.


01:01:26.379 --> 01:01:29.507
Any soldier that dies today
will live on in history.


01:01:29.582 --> 01:01:30.571
Press on.


01:01:44.430 --> 01:01:45.693
Closing in on target.


01:01:48.735 --> 01:01:50.760
Closing. Closing.


01:01:52.940 --> 01:01:54.601
It's a trap!


01:02:02.684 --> 01:02:05.847
There's too many! I need backup!


01:02:15.530 --> 01:02:16.964
They're coming straight at me!


01:02:17.032 --> 01:02:18.966
Help! I need help!
I need backup!


01:02:41.090 --> 01:02:43.889
- Launch terraformer.
- Aye, sir.


01:02:54.105 --> 01:02:55.093
No.


01:03:25.469 --> 01:03:27.734
Brace yourselves, men.


01:03:38.650 --> 01:03:40.845
What is that?


01:03:49.328 --> 01:03:50.659
Now.


01:03:59.907 --> 01:04:01.464
Senn?


01:04:01.542 --> 01:04:03.476
It's really happening.


01:04:12.052 --> 01:04:15.715
0.5% of oxygen produced.


01:04:15.789 --> 01:04:21.022
1%, 3%, 5%.


01:04:21.095 --> 01:04:23.860
Half a million cubic pounds
of oxygen generated.


01:04:23.932 --> 01:04:25.263
Accelerate.


01:04:28.703 --> 01:04:31.331
Concentrate your forces
on destroying that machine.


01:04:31.406 --> 01:04:32.998
Follow me!


01:04:37.779 --> 01:04:40.943
Gunfighters approaching on your left.


01:04:41.951 --> 01:04:43.213
Mala, watch out.


01:04:47.490 --> 01:04:48.981
Senn, I need help!


01:04:54.396 --> 01:04:56.194
Mala, don't worry.
I'm right behind you.


01:05:05.575 --> 01:05:08.169
Production up to 7%.


01:05:08.245 --> 01:05:10.646
Minor damages on filters G through M.


01:05:10.714 --> 01:05:12.978
- Accelerate.
- Sir?


01:05:14.118 --> 01:05:17.110
Sir, production of oxygen
at an advanced rate could be risky.


01:05:17.187 --> 01:05:18.382
Do it!


01:05:23.260 --> 01:05:25.525
That's it! You're damaging it!


01:05:25.596 --> 01:05:28.326
General, we've lost air filters A through F.


01:05:28.399 --> 01:05:30.799
Production is down.


01:05:30.869 --> 01:05:33.269
Divert resources to the remaining filters.


01:05:33.338 --> 01:05:35.669
Accelerate to maximum.


01:05:35.741 --> 01:05:37.901
If we compress the terraforming process,


01:05:37.975 --> 01:05:40.877
we'll be leaving ourselves
extremely vulnerable to combustion.


01:05:40.946 --> 01:05:42.607
That is a direct order!


01:05:42.681 --> 01:05:44.546
- Follow it!
- Sir, yes, sir.


01:05:44.616 --> 01:05:46.584
Second wave, attack!


01:05:48.187 --> 01:05:50.519
Phase 1 up to 25%.


01:05:50.589 --> 01:05:54.026
1.2 million cubic pounds of oxygen generated.


01:05:54.092 --> 01:05:56.652
But the terraforming filters
are under a lot of strain.


01:05:56.728 --> 01:05:59.095
How long before the process is completed?


01:05:59.165 --> 01:06:02.190
In 12 minutes, the chain reaction
will be irreversible.


01:06:02.268 --> 01:06:03.929
Hang in there, beautiful.


01:06:08.675 --> 01:06:10.905
Call in the reinforcements.


01:06:10.977 --> 01:06:14.378
Orders received, General.
We're on our way.


01:06:14.448 --> 01:06:17.383
Lock and load, people.
It's crunch time.


01:06:24.490 --> 01:06:26.617
I can't shake this guy!


01:06:31.498 --> 01:06:34.092
Hang in there, Jim.
I got this one.


01:06:40.207 --> 01:06:41.766
Jim, are you okay?


01:06:41.843 --> 01:06:43.936
Yeah, I'm fine. Just a scrape.


01:06:46.314 --> 01:06:47.508
I've got a clean shot.


01:06:54.489 --> 01:06:55.923
Mala, hostiles from above.


01:07:03.132 --> 01:07:05.692
Sir, we're decimating the Terrian resistance.


01:07:05.767 --> 01:07:07.099
Good.


01:07:07.169 --> 01:07:10.605
Keep production at maximum.
Let's finish this.


01:07:43.641 --> 01:07:46.269
I see an opening. I'm going in.


01:07:52.483 --> 01:07:55.510
- Mala, I can't shake 'em!
- Hold on. I'll be right there.


01:08:08.300 --> 01:08:10.359
No! Senn!


01:08:20.313 --> 01:08:21.610
No! No!


01:08:27.087 --> 01:08:28.384
No!


01:08:32.460 --> 01:08:35.293
Enemy fighter on my tail.
I need backup.


01:08:36.629 --> 01:08:38.791
Hang tight. I'm on my way.


01:08:39.933 --> 01:08:43.164
Sir, 90% of oxygen dispersed.


01:08:43.236 --> 01:08:45.671
Five minutes until completion of campaign.


01:08:53.647 --> 01:08:55.809
- You?
- Oh, no.


01:09:02.990 --> 01:09:04.389
Jim, where are you?


01:09:06.728 --> 01:09:09.698
Just hold on, Stewart.
I'm almost there.


01:09:09.765 --> 01:09:12.758
Mala? What?


01:09:23.311 --> 01:09:25.007
Jim, what are you doing?
Just shoot!


01:09:33.890 --> 01:09:36.189
I can't hold on much longer! Shoot!


01:09:54.746 --> 01:09:57.270
What are you doing, Jim?


01:10:02.921 --> 01:10:05.788
Wait, wait, wait! Jim!


01:10:05.857 --> 01:10:09.293
Incoming, sir!
It's one of ours!


01:10:09.360 --> 01:10:12.022
Stanton?
Pull away. Pull away!


01:10:14.233 --> 01:10:15.825
Fire at that ship!


01:12:01.477 --> 01:12:02.740
Come on!


01:13:15.322 --> 01:13:17.916
- Congratulations, Mala.
- Good job.


01:13:22.263 --> 01:13:26.222
Mala! Mala!


01:13:27.235 --> 01:13:28.862
Senn!


01:13:31.606 --> 01:13:32.868
- Mala.
- I thought you were dead.


01:13:32.940 --> 01:13:35.636
Oh, me, too.
I mean, you, too.


01:13:35.710 --> 01:13:39.511
You did well, Mala.
Very well.


01:13:39.580 --> 01:13:41.378
It wasn't me.


01:13:41.450 --> 01:13:43.713
He saved us.


01:13:43.785 --> 01:13:45.754
He saved us all.


01:13:45.821 --> 01:13:50.281
But now they have no food,
no water, no air.


01:13:50.359 --> 01:13:53.920
There's nothing for them to do
but just wait for the end.


01:13:53.996 --> 01:13:56.521
Never lose hope, Mala.


01:13:56.598 --> 01:13:59.466
There are always alternatives.


01:14:22.492 --> 01:14:25.086
- Hey, Senn.
- Hey, what?


01:14:25.161 --> 01:14:27.426
Race you.


01:14:27.498 --> 01:14:30.899
I knew you were gonna say that.
I don't know why I even answered.

